martinmunk-alsa-control-avr (0.3.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * avr-cec-relay: re-assert the TV demand on every TV-power poll while
    the TV is on, so the receiver recovers its input after an avr-
    controld restart (previously only sent on a TV state change). Pairs
    with the daemon acting on demand activation edges.

 -- Martin Munk Hansen <skiers.56.haggis@icloud.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 09:31:31 +0000

martinmunk-alsa-control-avr (0.3.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Denon IP: recover from a dropped telnet session. The receiver closes idle
    sessions; the long-lived avr-controld kept the dead socket and every
    command failed until restart (no volume/input control on StueTaerten).
    Now detects the close before each send, reconnects and re-sends.
  * Denon IP: volume/mute/power/input reads ask the receiver instead of a
    cache (the remote and HDMI-CEC change it too). get_power no longer
    reports "connected" as "on".
  * Input selection is per session again: the "input" parameter is exposed as
    the read-only "Input Source Default" element and applied by avr-power on,
    which selects it BEFORE powering on (Denon powers on straight into a
    non-HDMI input; PWON with an HDMI input selected wakes source + TV over
    CEC, which then grab the receiver). avr-power restore no longer switches
    the input back when it is about to power off, for the same reason.
  * Tests: mock XDROP/XDROPOTHERS hooks; reconnect, live-read and
    configured-input tests at integration and broker level.
  * avr-controld: optional shairport-sync D-Bus integration (sd-bus). With
    config "dbus=drive" the daemon watches shairport's play/pause and
    now-playing metadata on the system bus and, when playback starts, powers
    the AVR on and selects the configured input -- verifying via its own live
    reads that the receiver actually got there and retrying -- then powers off
    after a grace period (default 120s) once playback stops, so brief pauses
    and track gaps do not thrash the receiver. "dbus=observe" logs the events
    without touching the AVR; "dbus=off" (the default) is unchanged behaviour.
    Enable per node via /etc/avr-controld.conf. The ALSA volume/mute path is
    untouched. New socket verbs META and PLAYSTATE expose now-playing.
    New build dep: libsystemd-dev (runtime libsystemd0, already present).

 -- Martin Munk Hansen <hansen@martinmunk.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0000

martinmunk-alsa-control-avr (0.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add avr-controld: a single-owner connection broker. One daemon owns each
    AVR connection (serial/TCP) and serves clients over a Unix socket; the
    ALSA plugins become socket clients (SocketClientBackend) that auto-spawn
    it. Fixes per-process connection scoping (serial contention, TCP churn,
    no shared state). No plugin/avr-power source change.

 -- Martin Munk Hansen <hansen@martinmunk.com>  Sun, 09 Aug 2026 21:51:35 +0000

martinmunk-alsa-control-avr (0.2.6) stable; urgency=medium

  * Install the ALSA plugins into the host arch's multiarch dir via
    GNUInstallDirs (CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR). The old detection hardcoded x86_64
    and otherwise used /usr/lib/alsa-lib, so arm64/cross builds installed to a
    directory libasound does not search.

